From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] comdlg32: redraw the file list after giving it the dialog's font

Purpose: make the open and save dialogs select the file that was clicked
when the list's own font and the dialog's font have different heights.
Windows behavior: a list view that gets WM_SETFONT with redraw FALSE keeps
what it has drawn; the caller is to redraw it.
Wine before: the dialog created the shell view (which drew its list in the
list's default font, the icon title font) and then set the dialog's font
without redrawing. When the two fonts' heights differ, the rows stayed on
screen at the old height while clicks and later drawing used the new one,
so a click on the lower half of a row selected the next file, and a
selected row was drawn over its neighbour.
Change: set the font with redraw TRUE.
Evidence: in a Windows 7 shell prefix (icon title font Meiryo 9pt, rows
19 px; dialog font rows 17 px) clicking plain.txt selected the file below
it; with the change, the rows are drawn 17 px apart and the clicked file
is selected. +listview showed the paint before WM_SETFONT.
Scope: comdlg32's explorer-style open and save dialogs; the list is drawn
once more when it is created.
---
 dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c b/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c
index b00951a..476bc20 100644
--- a/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c
+++ b/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c
@@ -417,7 +417,9 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI IShellBrowserImpl_BrowseObject(IShellBrowser *iface,
 
     /* Set view window control id to 5002 */
     SetWindowLongPtrW(hwndView, GWLP_ID, lst2);
-    SendMessageW( hwndView, WM_SETFONT, SendMessageW( GetParent(hwndView), WM_GETFONT, 0, 0 ), FALSE );
+    /* The view has already drawn its list in the list's own font, whose item
+     * height may differ from the dialog font's: redraw it. */
+    SendMessageW( hwndView, WM_SETFONT, SendMessageW( GetParent(hwndView), WM_GETFONT, 0, 0 ), TRUE );
 
     /* Select the new folder in the Look In combo box of the Open file dialog */
     FILEDLG95_LOOKIN_SelectItem(fodInfos->DlgInfos.hwndLookInCB,fodInfos->ShellInfos.pidlAbsCurrent);
